      "html": "<div class=\"pyq-source-text\">Let f : N → N and g : N → N be functions over the set N of natural numbers. We<br>   will say:<br><br>    • f (n) = O(g(n)) if there exist natural numbers c and x0 such that f (n) ≤ c g(n)<br>      for all n ≥ x0<br>    • f (n) = 2O(g(n)) if there exist natural numbers c and x0 such that f (n) ≤ 2(c g(n))<br>      for all n ≥ x0 .<br><br>  Consider the following statements<br><br>                         (I) 3n = O(2n )               (II) 3n = 2O(n)<br><br>  (a) Both (I) and (II) are true                  (b) (I) is true and (II) is false<br>  (c) (I) is false and (II) is true               (d) Both (I) and (II) are false</div>",
