      "html": "<div class=\"pyq-source-text\">Rohit and Ben participate in a new toss system introduced by the ICC. The umpire<br>   repeatedly tosses a fair coin (which comes up heads with probability 21 and tails with<br>   probability 12 ), until one of them wins. Rohit wins if the result of two consecutive<br>   tosses is heads (i.e., the pattern HH is seen), while Ben wins if the pattern TH is seen.<br>   What are the winning probabilities for Rohit and Ben?<br>   (a) 41 and 34            (b) 14 and 14            (c) 12 and 12             (d) 13 and 23</div>",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.cmi.ac.in/admissions/sample-qp/pgcs2024-solutions.pdf",
